{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>The price of silver</b> — exchange, like 'the price of this silver.' In my opinion, מחיר means exchange and barter, and it appears [to be] from the day that passed [i.e., from a root meaning 'to pass over']. And likewise the interpretation of 'the face of your flock' is those which set their faces to go there." "<b>Set your heart</b> — so that you not forget them. And do not set your heart to a high station, for treasure and kingship do not endure forever. Behold the grasses and herbage will be gathered with you and be food for your flock, and the sheep will be for your clothing, and the he-goats in exchange for a field, and the fat as the matter of your food, and the food of your household, and life by which your young women will live."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The bracketed editorial insertion [i.e., from a root meaning 'to pass over'] is an attempt to render Ibn Ezra's compressed etymological note, which links מחיר to the root חרה/עבר in the sense of 'passing over' or 'exchange.' The phrase ונראה מהיום שעבר is textually compressed and its syntax is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:08.922948244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}